{title: The Request For Abishag}
{subtitle: 1 Kings 1:1–4; 1:5–7; 1:32–35; 2:13–17; 2:19–25}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
| [Gm] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Old King David could not get warm
Ser[Eb]vants searched for a young girl
They found [Cm]Abishag of Shunem
She served him with [Gm]gentle care
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Adonijah claimed he would be king
He took [Eb]chariots and horsemen
Fifty [Cm]men ran ahead of him
But the [Gm]kingdom was not his
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ask for Abishag as your wife
[Eb]This request hides a deadly claim
[Cm]Solomon sees through the veil of lies
The [Gm]throne is not yours to claim
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Zadok and Nathan anoint the heir
At [Eb]Gihon the trumpet sounds
Long live King [Cm]Solomon they shout
The suc[Gm]cession is now secure
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Adonijah goes to Bathsheba
[Eb]He speaks with a humble face
But [Cm]his heart desires the crown
He [Gm]tests the new King's grace
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Why do you ask for her as wife
[Gm]Ask for the kingdom as well
For [Eb]Joab and Abiathar too
This word [D]will cost your life [Gm]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Benaiah strikes Adonijah down
He [Eb]dies for his greed
The old King's [Cm]care becomes a trap
In the [Gm]court's dark deed
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm] | [Cm] | [Gm] | ×2
| [Gm] |
